      "description": "Watch Cambridge United vs Millwall highlights and goals from Carabao on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 25, 2026. The Carabao Cup returned with high intensity on August 25, 2026 , as Cambridge United hosted Millwall in a clash that promised tactical intrigue and knockout drama. Both sides entered the pitch looking to secure their place in the next round of the competition. Early Dominance and the Breakthrough Millwall started the match with aggressive intent, putting the home side under immediate pressure. The visitors came agonizingly close to an opener in the 7th minute when Lyndon Dykes struck the crossbar following a clinical fast break. The momentum stayed with the Lions, and just two minutes later, they found the net. After a corner delivered by Zak Lovelace , Jake Cooper saw his first effort hit the woodwork before reacting quickest to slot a left-footed shot into the bottom right corner. Cambridge United fought to find a way back into the game before the break. Gassan Ahadme narrowly missed the target with a header from a Sullay Kaikai cross, while Ra'ees Bangura-Williams forced a sharp save from Jake Eastwood at the other end. The first half concluded with the visitors holding a slender but deserved lead. A Late Surge and Defensive Resilience In the second half, the hosts introduced Louis Appéré to add more attacking threat. However, their rhythm was disrupted by an injury to Patrick Bauer , who was replaced by Callum Perry shortly after receiving a yellow card. Despite the setback, Cambridge United began to dominate possession, with Glenn McConnell and Shayne Lavery both coming close to an equalizer in the final twenty minutes. As the clock ticked into six minutes of added time, the tension at the stadium reached its peak. Callum Perry unleashed a powerful shot toward the center of the goal, but Millwall keeper Max Crocombe remained alert to make a crucial save. Despite a late flurry of corners and a final free kick won by Lohan McDougald , Millwall held firm to protect their 1-0 advantage and advance to the next round."
